# ─── Build outputs ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Regenerated on every `npm run resume`. Each user produces their
# own; never check these in. The PDFs are named after whoever built
# them (Gaius_Caesar_Resume.pdf) and are written into dist/ alongside
# the HTML and other build artifacts — one more reason the whole
# directory stays out of the repository.
dist/

# ─── Private data ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# AN ALLOWLIST, NOT A DENYLIST. Everything under data/ is yours and
# stays on this machine; the three shipped templates are the only
# exceptions, and they are named one by one below.
#
# This used to list the private files individually, which meant a new
# file in data/ was committed unless someone remembered to add a line
# for it — and several did slip through that way. Inverting it makes
# the failure mode "I have to un-ignore my template" instead of "my
# phone number is on GitHub".
#
# Renaming a data file therefore cannot expose it, and neither can
# moving it into a subfolder such as data/legacy/. Only adding a
# `!data/..._default.yml` line can, and that is a deliberate act.
#
# `data/**` rather than `data/*.yml`: a `*` stops at a slash, so the
# narrower pattern left every file in a subfolder committable.
data/**

# The shipped placeholders, so a fresh clone still builds.
!data/resume_default.yml
!data/letter_default.yml
!data/_profile_default.yml

# Snapshot fixtures built from your data. The committed ones
# (expected_resume-color.pdf, expected_resume-grayscale.pdf) come from
# the template and stay tracked.
tests/fixtures/expected_resume-color.mine.pdf
tests/fixtures/expected_resume-grayscale.mine.pdf
# The same two files under their pre-rename names. Nothing writes
# these any more, but a copy made before the rename is a render of
# your real resume.
tests/fixtures/*.local.pdf

# ─── Assistant output ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Files an AI assistant saves into the project folder: preview
# renders, drafts, comparisons. They are made from YOUR data — a
# render of your letter shows your name, phone number and email — so
# they are private for exactly the reason data/ is.
Claude outputs/

# ─── Test artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Diff images written when a snapshot test fails. They're useful
# for debugging the failure but shouldn't pollute history.
# Pattern matches diff_color_pageN.png and diff_grayscale_pageN.png.
tests/fixtures/diff_*.png

# ─── Python ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
# Virtual environments, in case you ever spin one up.
venv/
.venv/
env/
# Coverage artifacts.
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*

# ─── Node ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reinstalled by `npm install` from package-lock.json.
node_modules/
# Test coverage artifacts.
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# ─── Secrets / environment overrides ────────────────────────────
# Defensive — not currently used, but a common Git footgun.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ─── Logs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# ─── Editor / OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Editor settings, except the one that is part of the project.
#
# .vscode/settings.json maps schemas/ onto data/, which is what gives
# the YAML files completion and inline validation — and what turns off
# SchemaStore, without which `resume.yml` draws errors from the
# unrelated JSON Resume spec. Someone cloning this needs it, so it is
# committed; everything else under .vscode/ is per-machine noise.
#
# NOTE the trailing /* rather than /. Git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded — it never descends into it — so
# `.vscode/` followed by `!.vscode/settings.json` silently ignores the
# file anyway. Excluding the directory's contents instead leaves git
# free to walk in and honor the exception.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.bak
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ─── Desktop shell (Resume Studio) ───────────────────────────────
# Rust build artifacts. `npm run studio` fills this with several GB
# of compiled crates on the first run; none of it is source.
src-tauri/target/

# Bundled installers produced by `npm run studio:build`.
src-tauri/gen/

# Studio no longer writes to data/ at all, but old timestamped copies
# may still be lying around. Covered by `data/*.yml.bak` and the
# blanket `*.bak` above; kept explicit so the intent survives a tidy-up.
data/*.yml.*.bak
